   <indicator ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">WSH-R2: Number of people having access to dignified, safe, clean and functional excreta disposal facilities</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access: ratio (user/facility) of 1 toilet for a max. 20 people, distance &lt; 50 metres from dwellings, or as locally agreed. 
Clean: regular cleaning and maintenance for public facilities.
Dignified: Use of toilets respect cultural preference and is arranged by household(s) and/or segregated by sex. 
Unsafe facilities: unstable (unlined) pits with risk of collapse, pits accessible to vectors, pits contaminating water tables and poorly sited facilities which expose women and girls to attacks, especially at night. 
Functional facility: fully constructed, in working order and properly maintained, of a type and in a location acceptable to intended users, with hand washing facilities and anal cleansing material.</narrative>
    </description>
